From: BaresipKit <baresipkit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:32:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] audio: open the NAT pinhole for receive-only audio

The natpinhole account option sends empty RTP packets while a stream
only receives, so that NATs and media relays that learn the endpoint
from the first packet (such as rtpengine) can forward the peer's media.
Only video used it. Early media previews are typically audio recvonly,
and stay silent behind such relays. Open the pinhole for receive-only
audio as well; it stops when the first RTP packet arrives or the
direction changes.
---
 src/audio.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/audio.c b/src/audio.c
index e42f963..a10a61e 100644
--- a/src/audio.c
+++ b/src/audio.c
@@ -1230,6 +1230,11 @@ int audio_update(struct audio *a)
 		stop_tx(&a->tx, a);
 	}
 
+	if (dir == SDP_RECVONLY)
+		stream_open_natpinhole(a->strm);
+	else
+		stream_stop_natpinhole(a->strm);
+
 	if (a->tx.ac && aurecv_codec(a->aur)) {
 
 		if (!a->started) {

